& [RegistryImplementation] is content addressed
  + [procedures] are resolve SOP subject, inspect identity boundary, and review attention transition
  + [verification] is exact envelope, unique identities, closed schemas, empty effects, contained source paths, source hashes, normalized contract hashes, and ordered catalogue hash
  + [dependency_pins] are Needle package and baked engine plus Cantor executable, fixture environment, and query template SHA-256 values
  + [check_use_boundary] reloads and rehashes the catalogue after learned selection before execution
  + [deployment_manifest] pins ten controller, wrapper, contract, suite, lockfile, documentation, and test artifacts and is verified before every public command

& [SelectionImplementation] is advisory and fail closed
  + [Needle] receives only verified tool schemas and one caller stimulus
  + [execution_boundary] starts one child worker for each learned selection, re-verifies package and engine identity in that child, and terminates it after the parent-configured 30-second deadline
  + [system_field] is omitted because Needle defines it as environment facts rather than instruction steering
  + [purpose] is bound to the exact caller stimulus by the host instead of model paraphrase
  + [encoding_separation] canonical sorted JSON is reserved for identity and hash formation while compact order-preserving JSON carries declared tool schema order into the learned model
  + [gate] requires successful generation, exactly one known call, finite calibrated confidence at least 0.65, grounded non-negated validation, and schema-valid arguments
  + [no_call] is an explicit no_procedure_selected fault and never falls through to Cantor

& [CantorImplementation] is the authority seam
  + [invocation] is the existing strict cantor.exe query subprocess protocol
  + [proof_gate] requires successful protocol and query outcomes, empty faults, verified expected packages, at least one verified source quote, and matching inner and outer result digests
  + [frame] carries procedure and catalogue identity, caller attribution, verified semantic projection, proof references, boundary account, attention directive, and limitations

& [ArticulationImplementation] is one clean return pass
  + [provider] is the existing unmodified loopback llama.cpp server with Qwen3.5-0.8B
  + [request] contains the caller stimulus and one AttentionFrame but no tools, tool choice, or parallel-tool declaration
  + [reasoning_control] uses chat_template_kwargs enable_thinking false and reasoning_effort none
  + [attention_compression] projects only resolved subjects, verified quotes, boundary account, result digest, procedure identity, caller arguments, directive, and limitations; bulky proof internals remain in the archived Cantor response
  + [output_grammar] uses llama.cpp response_format schema constraint for one conclusion enum and one to six short dimension-tagged findings, then host-groups them into preserved, added, removed, conflicting, unsupported, and unresolved arrays
  + [output] is schema-valid bounded unsigned provider output; semantic correctness is not inferred from schema compliance

& [EvidenceImplementation] is staged and inspectable
  + [files] are 00 input, 01 sanitized selection, 02 Cantor response, 03 AttentionFrame, 04 sanitized provider response, result, and manifest when each stage exists
  + [manifest] binds every prior file by byte count and SHA-256
  + [privacy] recursively removes conventional model-private reasoning fields
  + [faults] retain typed public cause, run identity, stage evidence, and no traceback
  + [evaluation] validates a bounded versioned route-only suite, retains every constituent run, emits one hashed summary, and exits nonzero on any unexpected route or refusal
  + [negative_semantics] permits only an explicit closed set of policy-equivalent typed refusal codes where non-execution is the contract and one learned failure mechanism is not
  + [reverification] accepts one canonical UUID, resolves exactly one run or evaluation, rehashes the exact manifested file set, rejects missing or extra files, and binds result identity plus status to the manifest without rerunning inference

& [CalibrationCorrections] are preserved
  + [first] required free-text purpose and an instructional Needle system field produced confidence 0.0039 and were replaced by source-versioned host purpose binding
  + [second] generic thinking false was ignored by llama.cpp and exhausted the response budget in reasoning; supported template and effort controls fixed articulation
  + [third] sorting schema keys for canonical hashing also altered the model-visible token sequence and reduced correct-route confidence from 0.8154 to 0.4665; model transport now preserves declared schema order without weakening canonical identity
  + [fourth] an initial transition fixture overspecified low confidence even though a no-call response fulfilled the same fail-closed contract; the evaluator now distinguishes policy outcome from a closed set of learned refusal mechanisms
  + [fifth] explicit procedure and field names activated identity at 0.8407 and transition at 0.7201 without a threshold change, proving a viable structured-ingress attention language while ordinary paraphrases remain incompletely calibrated
  + [sixth] an initial structured output let a free summary absorb findings or repeat until truncation; compact projection plus conclusion-and-findings grammar removed that escape path

